\subsection{Definitions and mathematical statement}
\paragraph{Statement recorded in the supplied source.}
Is there a universal C such that, for each $0<\varepsilon <1$, every self-adjoint x in a complex von Neumann algebra M and every MASA $A\subseteq M$ can be strongly approximated by self-adjoint y of norm $\leq 3||x||$, with a partition $(p_i)$ in A into at most $C\varepsilon ^-6$ pieces and a self-adjoint $a\in A$ of norm $\leq ||y||$ satisfying $||\sum p_iyp_i-a||\leq \varepsilon ||y||$? No separability or expectation is assumed.

\subsection{Short English statement}
Is there a universal C such that, for each $0<\varepsilon <1$, every self-adjoint x in a complex von Neumann algebra M and every MASA $A\subseteq M$ can be strongly approximated by self-adjoint y of norm $\leq 3||x||$, with a partition $(p_i)$ in A into at most $C\varepsilon ^-6$ pieces and a self-adjoint $a\in A$ of norm $\leq ||y||$ satisfying $||\sum p_iyp_i-a||\leq \varepsilon ||y||$? No separability or expectation is assumed.

\subsection{Sources}
\begin{itemize}
\item[S1] OpenAI, manuscript citation page. Source of the formulation motivating this local problem.
\url{https://github.com/openai/math/blob/adc7f1241b42e322a6451854ab7e4b4c146bf78a/preprints/Approximation-Paving-over-Arbitrary-Maximal-Abelian-Subalgebras-September-25-2026/README.md}.
\end{itemize}

